==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 8~20 seconds<sup>240f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 8~20 seconds<sup>240f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 8~20 seconds<sup>240f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 8~20 seconds<sup>240f~600f</sup>.
**3 [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
At the start, use [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Giraffe Cats]] sparingly and save up money. After the first Celeboodle appears, It's your choice what to do: Using [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Mythical Titan Cat]] can deal with many of the enemies. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] is also recommended, being able to take on many enemies at once. With the proper support, [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cat]] may be used. Cheap rares such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] are able to beat the stage easily.

Alternatively, if [[Empire of Cats|Empire of Cats 3]] is uncleared, [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] can be used along with [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] to deal high amounts of damage. [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|True Valkyrie Cat]] is used here instead of Bahamut Cat. Paris Cat is still useful here, along with Titan Cat.

